(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The dispatch loop (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): one loop per entry from Go, running frames until"] [4 1 "// the entry frame returns. A call of a Python function pushes its frame and continues; a return pops"] [5 1 "// it. An exception unwinds by the exception table: the covering handler's depth, lasti and target,"] [6 1 "// else the frame is left and the caller's instruction raises it."] [8 1 "// guardedStep is step with a Go panic of the runtime turned into a SystemError raised at f's instruction"] [9 1 "// (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core, PY6a's Low: a panic ended the whole lib-test module, now only its test)"] [14 31 "// the C-level checks' increments the panic skipped"] [15 31 "// and a direct call's (queue 216d), had the panic crossed one"] [20 3 "// step's own frame not entered for compiled code (queue 216d); while tracing, the loop (queue 219t): a compiled"] [21 3 "// frame hands itself over at a block start (AotToLoop)"] [29 1 "// runResumed is run for a generator's frame sent into after a yield (queue 594): the eval breaker's error of its RESUME"] [30 1 "// raised in the frame at its resumption, where the generator's own handlers take it, as CPython's RESUME in the"] [31 1 "// generator raises it (a frame suspended at a yield-from is not checked, as RESUME_AFTER_YIELD_FROM: its delegate is; _testcapi's"] [32 1 "// raise_SIGINT_then_send_None, bpo-30039: the KeyboardInterrupt caught in the innermost generator)."] [42 3 "// entered as runFrames enters it, past a RESUME that checks nothing: the yield-from goes on to its delegate"] [62 1 "// run runs f (and the frames it calls) to f's return: Go's call into the machine, CPython's"] [63 1 "// _PyEval_EvalFrameDefault entered from C, the C level's recursion check first (where \"\", PY7)."] [75 1 "// runFrames is run's loop, f its entry frame. direct (queue 216d): f is a callee a compiled caller runs from its own Go"] [76 1 "// code (callDirect) where it would have returned f as its *pushFrame: f entered as this loop enters a pushed frame,"] [77 1 "// the eval breaker's error raised in f, and no C level counted (a Python call is none: run's check is Go's entry)."] [81 18 "// f_back of an escaped frame reaches its callers (202b)"] [89 31 "// a direct callee's RESUME error, raised in it as in a pushed frame"] [90 31 "// RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go)"] [99 41 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW (queue 220; breakMonitor)"] [107 1 "// loop is runFrames's loop from its entry frame f, entered (f_back, the depth, the thread's frame) and past its RESUME:"] [108 1 "// pending, when not nil, is the error f's first step raises (queue 330: a generator's frame goes on here from its"] [109 1 "// yield-from once its delegate, resumed by resume itself, is done)."] [119 37 "// PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD (queue 220): a callback's error raised in f"] [123 5 "// a jump (f_lineno) from the yield's event: the frame goes on there, the value not yielded"] [124 5 "// (INSTRUMENTED_YIELD_VALUE's frame->instr_ptr check; queue 281: test_sys_settrace's test_jump_from_yield)"] [130 4 "// f returned v"] [138 21 "// a suspended generator's f_back is None (its caller may be reused: releaseFrame)"] [149 5 "// callInit's __init__ returned: the instance is the call's value (type_call's check of __init__'s)"] [156 4 "// the moment at a frame's return (finAtReturn): one load and a compare while no object with a __del__"] [157 4 "// made by a frame this deep is waiting"] [167 4 "// a call of a Python function from f: run the callee in this loop. The thread's reused signal lets go of the"] [168 4 "// callee once taken (py-regress-1126: it held the last frame pushed, an __init__'s with its instance, from outside"] [169 4 "// the collection's graph, so a cycle through it was never garbage: test_traceback's test_print_traceback_at_exit;"] [170 4 "// py-mp-1125, the same fix: an escaped frame's locals, sys._getframe(0)'s or a warning's f_back, outlived the"] [171 4 "// frame's return and a gc.collect)"] [188 5 "// the callee's RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go), its error raised in the callee; then"] [189 5 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START (queue 220: breakMonitor keeps the breaker set while a tool has events)"] [200 3 "// an exception in f at f.Lasti"] [206 4 "// an exception the runtime raised in f (a KeyError of d[k] ...): chained as _PyErr_SetObject chains"] [211 40 "// a re-raise adds no entry for the frame it is raised in (exception_unwind)"] [212 40 "// RERAISE (queue 281: monitor_reraise)"] [220 41 "// END_ASYNC_FOR's RERAISE (queue 281)"] [223 45 "// RAISE (queue 219t): settrace's 'exception'"] [228 43 "// EXCEPTION_HANDLED (queue 281: monitor_handled)"] [235 40 "// a for loop's fresh generator the exception leaves (queue 339)"] [240 47 "// frame->instr_ptr: a reraise N's restored instruction"] [246 24 "// PY_UNWIND (queue 220)"] [248 6 "// the handler CPython wraps a generator's body in (codegen's STOPITERATION_ERROR and RERAISE; queue 281)"] [254 24 "// the frame cleared: its for loops' fresh generators closed (queue 339)"] [267 1 "// OpImpl implements an operation outside step's switch (PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): it pops and pushes f's"] [268 1 "// stack itself and returns (nil, nil) to go on; (nil, err) raises; (nil, *pushFrame) runs a Python"] [269 1 "// function's frame next; (v, nil) makes f return v (a generator's yield sets f.Suspended first)."] [272 1 "// opImpls are the operations registered by the files that own them (§9), each by its file's init:"] [273 1 "// RegisterOp(OpLoadAttr, ...). An operation of step's switch is never looked up here."] [276 1 "// RegisterOp sets op's implementation; a second one is a programming error (one owner per operation)."] [284 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [287 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [288 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [289 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [290 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [294 22 "// sys.monitoring's CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [306 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [319 4 "// a built-in method bound to its object (BuiltinType's call slot): its arguments made at once with self"] [320 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [336 51 "// next(gen()): the generator dies at the return (queue 297)"] [359 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [368 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [369 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [370 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [373 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [374 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect: its value pushed on f's stack, or its exception returned); else returned"] [375 1 "// as the thread's *pushFrame, read by runFrames before the thread's next call."] [384 1 "// callDirect runs callee, a compiled function's frame called by f's compiled code (queue 216d, the user's (a) on"] [385 1 "// 216's DECISION 1): a loop of its own (runFrames, direct) with callee its entry frame, entered as runFrames enters a"] [386 1 "// pushed frame (f_back f, the recursion limit's check raising in f, the eval breaker's error in callee, no C level),"] [387 1 "// so its exception unwinds throu